  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ae435a84-c5b8-5cc1-92c0-f0f48c41ca18" activityNameId="ab6d56c5-5eec-5f7f-82e9-23d952857bdc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Copper, secondary, at refinery</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Copper, secondary, at refinery
The module describes the production of secondary copper in Germany with a production of 176'000 t copper cathodes in 1994. It is designed for the use of the metal as part of the consumption mix "copper, at regional storage". It is not to be used if the impact of the secondary copper is considerable. In such cases, a more detailed analysis has to be conducted.;
UUID: 72090602-835f-3db2-b0dc-61366408f8ab
The module includes the collection and handling of the copper scrap, the refining and the processes for waste water treatment.
Location: This module is valid for one single very big plant, which is taken as proxy for the RER.
Technology: In three different stages different types of copper scrap and 10% of the feed of blister copper are refined to copper cathodes. Waste water is led to a communal treatment plant.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: Env. 50% of the 2.3 million tonnes = 1.2 million tonnes in STAF Europe in 1994.
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_72090602-835f-3db2-b0dc-61366408f8ab.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
